Package: baxters-iris
Version: 0.1.1
Section: video
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Baxters Lab <165753632+Baxterv5@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libegl1, libwayland-client0, libwayland-egl1, libxkbcommon0, libx11-6, libxcb1, libdbus-1-3
Description: Iris — USB camera capture with live telemetry
 Deterministic, telemetry-rich camera subsystem: V4L2 enumeration and streaming
 capture with MJPEG decode, a live preview, and a full outbound telemetry
 pipeline. Iris is a tool, not a brain — it performs no inference.
 .
 Depends were taken from the libraries a RUNNING instance actually maps, not
 from ldd alone: the binary links only libc6 and libgcc-s1, while eframe/winit
 dlopen EGL, Wayland and xkbcommon at startup. Declaring only the linked pair
 would install cleanly and then fail to open a window — the same defect found
 in Power Goo, whose Depends omitted qt6-wayland.
 .
 The GPU stack is deliberately NOT depended on. A live process also maps mesa,
 libdrm and the NVIDIA driver, but those are provided by whichever driver the
 host runs; libegl1 pulls the vendor-neutral libglvnd loader, which is the
 correct dependency for any of them.
